From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Zinc Lim <zinclim@meta.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 14:27:14 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] hw/misc/i2c-netdev2: opt out of short-frame padding

Since upstream f448e6d9cf ("net: Pad short packets consistently
regardless of backend"), qemu_send_packet() pads every frame shorter
than ETH_ZLEN unless the receiving NetClientState sets do_not_pad, and
the socket backend now does it too. A NIC from qemu_new_nic() does not
set it, so i2c-netdev2 got the peer's 2-byte ACK as a 60-byte frame:
not ACK_LEN, so it hit assert(len <= sizeof(s->rx_buf)) and QEMU
aborted on the first transaction.

The packet length is i2c-netdev2's framing (ACK, START, DATA, STOP and
read replies are told apart by size), so it must see the bytes the peer
sent. Opt out of the padding, as the commit says devices that handle
short packets should.
---
 hw/misc/i2c-netdev2.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/hw/misc/i2c-netdev2.c b/hw/misc/i2c-netdev2.c
index 67587b5f57..7f176cbd37 100644
--- a/hw/misc/i2c-netdev2.c
+++ b/hw/misc/i2c-netdev2.c
@@ -263,6 +263,8 @@ static void i2c_netdev2_realize(DeviceState *dev, Error **errp)
     s->bus = I2C_BUS(qdev_get_parent_bus(dev));
     s->nic = qemu_new_nic(&i2c_netdev2_client_info, &s->nic_conf, TYPE_I2C_NETDEV2,
                           dev->id, &dev->mem_reentrancy_guard, s);
+    /* Packet length is the protocol; padding to ETH_ZLEN would corrupt it. */
+    qemu_get_queue(s->nic)->do_not_pad = true;
     s->bh = qemu_bh_new(i2c_netdev2_slave_mode_rx, s);
     s->rx_len = 0;
 }
